Generated node:test checks later run directly in a read-only exported evaluation tree, with repository root as cwd, not the /workspace authoring checkout. Read repository files relative to process.cwd(), which is the repository root in every evaluation context. That tree has no .git, history, refs or index. Do not invoke Git to inspect the candidate or compare revisions. Network is unavailable. Assert actual contract behavior using available files and modules.

Trusted gates separately run baseline, main and candidate tests, typecheck, lint and format. Do not invoke npm run check or duplicate those aggregate gates inside held-out tests. Every contract criterion and assertion must remain covered; this evaluation context does not waive a criterion.

Checks must not use a module loader hook (node:module register or registerHooks), must not patch built-in modules, module internals or process members (exit, reallyExit, exitCode, on, once, addListener, prependListener, prependOnceListener) by assignment, delete, Object.defineProperty, Object.defineProperties, Object.assign, Object.setPrototypeOf, Reflect.defineProperty, Reflect.set, Reflect.setPrototypeOf or Reflect.deleteProperty, and must not attach a process exit, beforeExit or uncaughtException handler: the trusted tamper scan refuses such a suite before build. Do not patch other globals or prototypes, and do not use lint or type suppression comments such as @ts-ignore, @ts-expect-error, @ts-nocheck, eslint-disable, oxlint-disable or biome-ignore. Import the real modules and assert on their behavior instead.

