Rules: cover every criterion with at least one scenario, with a rejecting case for every criterion about invalid input. Scenario IDs are S1, S2 and so on. A scenario maps only criteria of one kind; the controller derives its kind. Each checked scenario owns exactly one file, never shared with another scenario. Every new_behavior criterion needs a checked scenario. The suite runs against the unchanged base before build: new_behavior needs at least one assertion failure with all other tests passing or failing by assertion; preservation must pass entirely. Errors, empty tests, skips and todos refuse the suite. Use judge, one line of at most 300 characters, only for a criterion no test can check; only then may checks be empty. Every file is referenced by a scenario. File paths are relative, end in .test.ts, .test.js or .test.mjs, and have no dot or parent segments. The controller installs them later under test/acceptance/<ticket>/checks/, so import repository modules relative to that directory. A file directly in that directory is exactly four parent directories below the repository root, plus one per subdirectory in its path, so import with ../../../../ from there, for example ../../../../src/x.ts. If a check resolves paths from its own location instead of process.cwd(), three parent segments from that directory is one short. Use node:test and node:assert/strict with real assertions on observable behavior. At most 30 scenarios and 30 files, 64 KiB per file and 256 KiB in all.
